1.If a neural network has only one hidden layer then neural network is called a perceptron.When we have multiple hidden layers for processing input layers data to
the output layer,then ANN is called deep learning.

2.Each input variable becomes the input node of the input layer of ANN,while number of output classes to be predicted becomes number of output nodes.

3.In case of regression and binary classification a single output node is used.

4.The neural network deals with only a single row at a time.

5.ANN model is very sensitive to input attributes so input data should be preprocessed(scale, encode etc) carefully.

6.By adjusting weights the neural network identifies importance of a signal from the neuron.

7. 3 Step Learning process of a neuron :
   i. Calculate weighted sum.
   ii. Apply activation function on weighted sum.Few types of activation function are:
      1.Threshold function      2.Sigmoid function 
      3.Rectified linear unit function      4.Hyperbolic tangent function
   iii. Signal is passed to next neighbouring neuron.
